   1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
   2: #
   3: #  #499 sgireunmapped -- the detector.
   4: #
   5: #  DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_re)'s final catch-all -- every offset in the 4 KB window
   6: #  matching none of the six address arms -- used to end the host process.  This
   7: #  round declines the access and announces it once per direction.  These rows
   8: #  pin the decline, its two latch bits, and the ACCEPT side of all six arms,
   9: #  which the removed exit(1) used to police by accident.
  10: #
  11: #  CONTRACT (vacuity-floor clause (e)) -- which edits this detector is designed
  12: #  to catch, and which it is NOT:
  13: #
  14: #    CATCHES
  15: #      * reinstatement of the catch-all host kill, in EITHER direction
  16: #        (`wr surv', `rd surv', and the `wr kill'/`rd kill' text rows).  Both
  17: #        directions are pinned because a repair qualified to writes only is the
  18: #        commonest partial: MEASURED at 11/14 on the artifact detector's
  19: #        `mwonly' variant;
  20: #      * a decline that returns `return 0', which cpus/memory_rw.c coerces to
  21: #        -1 and raises a guest EXCEPTION_DBE.  `rd sent' presets the
  22: #        destination register to a SENTINEL, so "the tail ran and wrote
  23: #        odata (0)" and "the load never completed" are distinguishable, and
  24: #        `rd nodbe' reads the exception channel directly.  A survival-only
  25: #        oracle at a refusal-effect site is vacuous by construction;
  26: #      * loss of either latch, so the decline floods (`wr lat1', `rd lat1'
  27: #        COUNT over two DIFFERENT offsets; presence would pass an unlatched
  28: #        build, and one offset twice would pass a per-address latch);
  29: #      * the two new bits COLLIDING with any of the seven that already exist.
  30: #        `xwin wr'/`xwin rd' walk all six #497 window latches AND sgi_de's
  31: #        #498 latch first, then take the catch-all: if a new bit is any of
  32: #        those seven, the announcement is silently suppressed.  MEASURED --
  33: #        the `fix6' variant, in which SGIRE_W_UNMAP_WR reuses 1 << 6 and so
  34: #        collides with #498's SGIRE_W_DE_LEN, escapes every other row here.
  35: #        The four sgi_re handlers share one malloc'd struct, so this is a
  36: #        cross-DEVICE collision, not merely a cross-window one, and a row
  37: #        walking only sgi_re's own windows would not have seen it;
  38: #      * the two new bits colliding with EACH OTHER (`wr rd 2msg'): one shared
  39: #        bit for both directions silences whichever comes second;
  40: #      * SHRINKING any window's FAR bound (the `acc hi' rows sit at each
  41: #        window's LAST legal 8-byte slot).  MEASURED at 13/14 each for TLB_A,
  42: #        TLB_B and TLB_C on the artifact detector;
  43: #      * GROWING any window's NEAR bound, and TRANSLATING a whole window.
  44: #        *** THIS IS THE HALF THE FIRST DRAFT DID NOT HAVE, AND IT WAS
  45: #        MEASURED MISSING RATHER THAN REASONED ABOUT. ***  A one-token edit --
  46: #        `>= CRIME_RE_LINEAR_A' to `>= CRIME_RE_LINEAR_A + 0x40' -- swept the
  47: #        14-row artifact detector CLEAN, because every accept row sat at its
  48: #        window's TOP slot, and a top-slot row tests the FAR bound and NEVER
  49: #        the near one.  A base-slot row has the mirrored blindness.  Both
  50: #        halves ship, per window;
  51: #      * MIS-ATTRIBUTION of an offset to the wrong arm, and re-mapping of a
  52: #        window's index arithmetic.  Every `acc' row matches the arm's own
  53: #        debug() text INCLUDING THE ARRAY NAME, THE INDEX AND THE VALUE --
  54: #        e.g. "d->re_tlb_a[252] = 0x1122" -- so it is anchored to a SPECIFIC
  55: #        CELL by a channel outside the decode under test, which is clause
  56: #        (f)'s requirement.  A "did not reach the catch-all" oracle cannot do
  57: #        this: it is satisfied by ANY arm servicing the access.
  58: #      * *** THE CATCH-ALL'S OWN STATE SPACE, ENUMERATED RATHER THAN PATCHED.
  59: #        Added by #499 pass 4 after THREE consecutive passes each found a breach
  60: #        of ONE class -- a cell of this space left empty, repaired at exactly the
  61: #        address the mutant had used, leaving the symmetric cell open for the
  62: #        next pass.  Two of the three were MEASURED CLEAN SWEEPS of a detector
  63: #        that had just come back green. ***
  64: #
  65: #        The catch-all's behaviour is a function of FIVE inputs, so they are
  66: #        listed and each is given a row that varies under a named mutant:
  67: #
  68: #          relative_addr  component 1 (0x16e0-0x16ff) and component 2 (0x1800+),
  69: #                         AND POSITION WITHIN a component.  Component 1 is a
  70: #                         32-byte RANGE, not a point: `>= CRIME_RE_LINEAR_A'
  71: #                         changed to `- 0x10' swept 36 rows CLEAN because all
  72: #                         four component-1 rows sat at the BASE.  `cliphi rd/wr'
  73: #                         sit at its LAST 8-byte slot (0x16f8);
  74: #          writeflag      `else if (relative_addr < CRIME_RE_LINEAR_A)' on the
  75: #                         READ arm also swept 36 rows clean -- component 1 was
  76: #                         probed by two sessions and BOTH were stores.
  77: #                         `clip rd *' and `cliphi rd *' close it;
  78: #          len            8 vs narrow, now at both components (`clip rdn *');
  79: #          idata          every write carried a NONZERO datum, so
  80: #                         `writeflag == MEM_WRITE && idata' had no disagreeing
  81: #                         row.  `wr zero surv'/`wr zero decl' supply one;
  82: #          d->warned      latch state at entry -- the `lat1' rows.
  83: #
  84: #        NOT COVERED IN THIS SPACE, deliberately and stated so a later escape is
  85: #        "outside the contract" rather than an argument about overclaiming:
  86: #          - component 1's LAST slot at NARROW width (the len axis is pinned at
  87: #            the base of both components and at neither far edge);
  88: #          - component 2's FAR edge.  It is bounded by DEV_SGI_RE_LENGTH rather
  89: #            than by a constant in this file, so the one-token shrink that works
  90: #            on component 1 has no analogue here;
  91: #          - a zero datum on the READ side (a read carries none) or at
  92: #            component 1.
  93: #
  94: #    DOES NOT CATCH
  95: #      * a collision among the SIX #497 window bits.  That is
  96: #        sgi_re_width_probe.py's `xsite 6msg' row, which is shipped and
  97: #        gate-wired, and which MEASURED 32/35 against the 1<<0 -> 1<<1 mutant
  98: #        built for this round.  Duplicating it here would add a row that can
  99: #        never fail alone;
 100: #      * the six `TODO: read from <sym>' kills, or sgi_de's drawing-op kill.
 101: #        Those are sgirekills and sgideprimop, deliberately untouched;
 102: #      * a change to the announcement's WORDING beyond the literals below;
 103: #      * anything in sgi_mte, or in sgi_de_status beyond the signature control.
 104: #
 105: #  *** THE ROW SET IS NOT INVENTED HERE.  Every row's mutant was built and
 106: #  scored before this file existed; the table, the variant diffs and the
 107: #  session transcripts are preserved under
 108: #  regress/artifacts/sgireunmapped/killtable_20260831/. ***
 109: #
 110: import os
 111: import pty
 112: import re
 113: import select
 114: import sys
 115: import time
 116: 
 117: BIN = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "build/gxemul"
 118: LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "local"
 119: 
 120: #  A load file is REQUIRED by -V ... 0x80001000:<file>, and this probe must not
 121: #  depend on a file sitting in an artifacts directory.  Same fallback as
 122: #  sgi_de_width_probe.py: the in-tree fixture if it exists, /dev/null if not.
 123: #  /dev/null is the live path today -- regress/dummy_kernel.bin is absent --
 124: #  and the guest never executes the loaded bytes anyway: every instruction this
 125: #  probe runs is written into RAM with `put w'.
 126: DUMMY = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "dummy_kernel.bin")
 127: if not os.path.exists(DUMMY):
 128:     DUMMY = "/dev/null"
 129: 
 130: CODE        = 0x80001000
 131: SCRATCH_RAM = 0xa0001800
 132: LIVE_VAL    = 0x12345678
 133: RE          = 0xb5001000          # sgi_re        @ phys 0x15001000
 134: DE          = 0xb5002000          # sgi_de        @ phys 0x15002000
 135: DE_STATUS   = 0xb5004000          # sgi_de_status @ phys 0x15004000
 136: DE_STAT_VAL = "0x1e000000"
 137: 
 138: #  Offsets past LINEAR_B's far bound, i.e. in the catch-all.  The latch rows
 139: #  use TWO DIFFERENT ones: one offset twice would pass a build that latched
 140: #  per-address instead of per-device.
 141: UNMAP_W  = 0x800
 142: UNMAP_W2 = 0x8c0
 143: UNMAP_R  = 0x900
 144: UNMAP_R2 = 0x9c0
 145: 
 146: ACC_VAL  = "0x1122334455667788"
 147: SENTINEL = 0xdeadbeef
 148: 
 149: 
 150: #  THE FULL LITERAL, WITH OUR OWN DATUM IN IT, IS THE POINT.
 151: #  A hand-assembled encoding with a wrong register field stores 0, and a row
 152: #  matching only "unimplemented write to address" would accept that.  Matching
 153: #  the echoed value makes the row un-fakeable the same way `devsig' is.
 154: #  The kill literal is NOT a substring of the decline literal -- the character
 155: #  after the datum is ' ]' in one and ' -' in the other -- so the two are
 156: #  mutually exclusive rather than merely different.
 157: def wr_decl(off, val=ACC_VAL):
 158:     #  #499 pass 4: `val' was hardcoded to ACC_VAL, so every row whose store used
 159:     #  a different datum -- the narrow rows, the zero-datum row -- had to fall back
 160:     #  to the bare substring "unimplemented write to address", which is ALSO a
 161:     #  prefix of the KILL text.  That abandons the mutual exclusivity the comment
 162:     #  above goes to trouble to establish.  Parameterised, those rows get the full
 163:     #  literal for free.
 164:     return ("unimplemented write to address 0x1%03x, data=%s -- declined."
 165:             "  (once) ]" % (off, val))
 166: 
 167: 
 168: def datum(val):
 169:     """the 16-hex-digit form the device prints for a t0 value of `val'"""
 170:     return "0x%016x" % int(val, 16)
 171: 
 172: 
 173: def wr_kill(off):
 174:     return "unimplemented write to address 0x1%03x, data=%s ]" % (off, ACC_VAL)
 175: 
 176: 
 177: def rd_decl(off):
 178:     return "unimplemented read from address 0x1%03x -- declined.  (once) ]" % off
 179: 
 180: 
 181: def rd_kill(off):
 182:     return "unimplemented read from address 0x1%03x ]" % off
 183: 
 184: 
 185: #  The six #497 width latches and #498's sgi_de latch -- the SEVEN bits the two
 186: #  new ones must not collide with.  Offsets are the window bases minus the
 187: #  handler's own `relative_addr += 0x1000'.
 188: PARTNERS = [
 189:     (RE + 0x000, "for CRIME_RE_TLB_A -- declined."),
 190:     (RE + 0x200, "for CRIME_RE_TLB_B -- declined."),
 191:     (RE + 0x400, "for CRIME_RE_TLB_C -- declined."),
 192:     (RE + 0x600, "for CRIME_RE_TEX -- declined."),
 193:     (RE + 0x700, "for CRIME_RE_LINEAR_A -- declined."),
 194:     (RE + 0x780, "for CRIME_RE_LINEAR_B -- declined."),
 195:     (DE + 0x0d0, "sgi_de: unimplemented len=1 -- declined."),
 196: ]
 197: 
 198: #  name   base   last 8-byte slot,  anchored text at base,  anchored text at last slot
 199: WINDOWS = [
 200:     ("tlba", 0x000, 0x1f8,
 201:      "d->re_tlb_a[0] = 0x1122", "d->re_tlb_a[252] = 0x1122"),
 202:     ("tlbb", 0x200, 0x3f8,
 203:      "d->re_tlb_b[0] = 0x1122", "d->re_tlb_b[252] = 0x1122"),
 204:     ("tlbc", 0x400, 0x5f8,
 205:      "d->re_tlb_c[0] = 0x1122", "d->re_tlb_c[252] = 0x1122"),
 206:     ("tex", 0x600, 0x6d8,
 207:      "d->re_tex[0] = 0x1122", "d->re_tex[27] = 0x1122"),
 208:     ("lina", 0x700, 0x778,
 209:      "[ d->re_linear_a[0] = 0x11223344, [1] = 0x55667788 ]",
 210:      "[ d->re_linear_a[30] = 0x11223344, [31] = 0x55667788 ]"),
 211:     ("linb", 0x780, 0x7f8,
 212:      "[ d->re_linear_b[0] = 0x11223344, [1] = 0x55667788 ]",
 213:      "[ d->re_linear_b[30] = 0x11223344, [31] = 0x55667788 ]"),
 214: ]
 215: 
 216: OP_NOP      = 0x00000000
 217: OP_B_SELF   = 0x1000ffff
 218: OP_SB_T0_A3 = 0xa0e80000          # sb   $t0, 0($a3)
 219: OP_SW_T0_A3 = 0xace80000          # sw   $t0, 0($a3)
 220: OP_SD_T0_A3 = 0xfce80000          # sd   $t0, 0($a3)
 221: OP_LW_V0_AT = 0x8c220000          # lw   $v0, 0($at)
 222: OP_LD_V0_AT = 0xdc220000          # ld   $v0, 0($at)
 223: 
 224: rows = []
 225: 
 226: 
 227: def row(name, got, want, note=""):
 228:     #  THE NAME COLUMN IS %-16s AND THE GATE'S PER-ROW PATTERN IS "^<name>  .*ok$"
 229:     #  -- TWO literal spaces.  A name of length L is followed by (16 - L) pad
 230:     #  characters plus the format's own space, so L must be <= 15 or the row emits
 231:     #  ONE space, the gate's check becomes UNSATISFIABLE (got=0 against want=1),
 232:     #  and the gate goes RED on a GREEN probe.
 233:     #
 234:     #  #499's pass 3 shipped exactly two 16-char rows and the failure was found by
 235:     #  a review seat rather than by the gate -- because the gate SCRIPT was never
 236:     #  run after they were added, only the probe.  Both were renamed to 13 chars.
 237:     #  This assert designs the trap out instead of asking the next author to
 238:     #  remember it.  Note the trap has an opposite form too: a name that is a
 239:     #  PREFIX of another matches two rows.
 240:     assert len(name) <= 15, (
 241:         "row name %r is %d chars; the gate pattern needs <= 15" % (name, len(name)))
 242:     ok = (got == want)
 243:     rows.append((name, ok))
 244:     print("%-16s %-14s %-14s %-48s %s" % (name, str(got), str(want), note,
 245:                                           "ok" if ok else "FAIL"))
 246:     return ok
 247: 
 248: 
 249: def session(cmds, settle=1.5, spin=1.2):
 250:     pid, fd = pty.fork()
 251:     if pid == 0:
 252:         os.execv(BIN, [BIN, "-V", "-x", "-E", "sgi", "-e", "ip32", "-M", "64",
 253:                        "0x80001000:" + DUMMY])
 254:         os._exit(127)
 255:     buf = ""
 256: 
 257:     def rd(t):
 258:         nonlocal buf
 259:         end = time.time() + t
 260:         while time.time() < end:
 261:             r, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0.1)
 262:             if not r:
 263:                 continue
 264:             try:
 265:                 d = os.read(fd, 65536)
 266:                 if not d:
 267:                     return False
 268:                 buf += d.decode("latin-1", "replace")
 269:             except OSError:
 270:                 return False
 271:         return True
 272: 
 273:     alive = rd(settle)
 274:     for i, c in enumerate(cmds):
 275:         try:
 276:             os.write(fd, (c + "\n").encode("latin-1"))
 277:         except OSError:
 278:             alive = False
 279:             break
 280:         if not rd(spin if i == len(cmds) - 1 else 0.25):
 281:             alive = False
 282:             break
 283:     try:
 284:         os.write(fd, b"quit\n")
 285:         rd(0.4)
 286:     except OSError:
 287:         pass
 288:     try:
 289:         os.close(fd)
 290:     except OSError:
 291:         pass
 292:     how = "nostatus"
 293:     try:
 294:         _, stat = os.waitpid(pid, 0)
 295:         if os.WIFSIGNALED(stat):
 296:             how = "sig%d" % os.WTERMSIG(stat)
 297:         elif os.WIFEXITED(stat):
 298:             how = "exit%d" % os.WEXITSTATUS(stat)
 299:     except OSError:
 300:         pass
 301:     return buf.replace("\r", ""), alive, how
 302: 
 303: 
 304: def printed(t, reg):
 305:     m = re.search(r"print\s+%s\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)" % reg, t)
 306:     if not m:
 307:         return "absent"
 308:     return "0x%x" % int(m.group(1), 16)
 309: 
 310: 
 311: class Addr(object):
 312:     """A FRESH code address per instruction sequence.
 313: 
 314:     *** THIS IS THE STRUCTURAL FORM OF A DEFECT THAT COST THE ARTIFACT
 315:     DETECTOR A ROW. ***  The gxprobe-based original cached register
 316:     assignments and skipped redundant ones; `step' advances pc, so a second
 317:     sequence written to the SAME address found pc already "set" there, the
 318:     assignment was skipped, and the guest executed the following nop instead
 319:     of the store.  Its `msg once' row then performed ONE access and two nops
 320:     and therefore COULD NOT FAIL -- a mutant that announced without ever
 321:     latching scored a clean sweep because of it.
 322: 
 323:     This file writes raw debugger commands with no cache, so an assignment can
 324:     never be skipped; handing out a distinct address per sequence additionally
 325:     keeps one sequence's dyntrans translation from being reached by the next.
 326:     The hazard is designed out rather than remembered.
 327:     """
 328: 
 329:     def __init__(self, base):
 330:         self.a = base
 331: 
 332:     def take(self, n):
 333:         got = self.a
 334:         self.a += 4 * (n + 2) + 0x20
 335:         return got
 336: 
 337: 
 338: def run_ops(ops, at):
 339:     put = ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * i, op) for i, op in enumerate(ops)]
 340:     put += ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * len(ops), OP_B_SELF),
 341:             "put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * len(ops) + 4, OP_NOP)]
 342:     return put + ["pc=0x%x" % at, "step %d" % len(ops)]
 343: 
 344: 
 345: def store(A, addr, op=OP_SD_T0_A3, val=ACC_VAL):
 346:     return ["a3=0x%x" % addr, "t0=%s" % val] + run_ops([op], A.take(1))
 347: 
 348: 
 349: def load(A, addr, op=OP_LD_V0_AT):
 350:     #  Preset to a SENTINEL, never to 0: preset to 0 a row cannot tell "the
 351:     #  common tail ran and wrote odata (0)" from "the load never completed".
 352:     return ["at=0x%x" % addr, "v0=0x%x" % SENTINEL] + run_ops([op], A.take(1))
 353: 
 354: 
 355: print("#499 sgireunmapped DETECTOR -- binary=%s label=%s" % (BIN, LABEL))
 356: print("%-16s %-14s %-14s %-48s %s" % ("row", "got", "want", "note", ""))
 357: 
 358: # ---------------------------------------------------------------- controls (c)
 359: A = Addr(CODE)
 360: t, alive, how = session(store(A, SCRATCH_RAM, OP_SW_T0_A3, "0x%x" % LIVE_VAL)
 361:                         + load(A, SCRATCH_RAM, OP_LW_V0_AT) + ["print v0"])
 362: row("live", printed(t, "v0") if alive else "died", "0x%x" % LIVE_VAL,
 363:     "LIVENESS: guest store then load, through RAM")
 364: 
 365: A = Addr(CODE)
 366: t, alive, how = session(load(A, DE_STATUS, OP_LW_V0_AT) + ["print v0"])
 367: row("devsig", printed(t, "v0") if alive else "died", DE_STAT_VAL,
 368:     "DEVSIG: CRIME_DE_STATUS reads 0x1e000000; RAM would read 0")
 369: 
 370: print("OPUS499T_CONTROL=%s" % ("OK" if all(o for _, o in rows) else "DEAD"))
 371: print("")
 372: 
 373: # ------------------------------------------------- the catch-all, WRITE side
 374: A = Addr(CODE)
 375: t, alive, how = session(store(A, RE + UNMAP_W))
 376: row("wr surv", how, "exit0", "unmapped WRITE: host survives")
 377: row("wr kill", t.count(wr_kill(UNMAP_W)), 0, "the pre-fix host kill text is gone")
 378: row("wr decl", t.count(wr_decl(UNMAP_W)), 1,
 379:     "the decline is announced, echoing OUR datum")
 380: 
 381: # ------------------------------------------------- the catch-all, READ side
 382: #  NOT redundant with the write rows: a repair qualified to writes only leaves
 383: #  this half dead.  MEASURED 11/14 on the artifact detector's `mwonly'.
 384: A = Addr(CODE)
 385: t, alive, how = session(load(A, RE + UNMAP_R) + ["print v0"])
 386: row("rd surv", how, "exit0", "unmapped READ: host survives")
 387: row("rd kill", t.count(rd_kill(UNMAP_R)), 0, "the pre-fix read kill text is gone")
 388: row("rd decl", t.count(rd_decl(UNMAP_R)), 1, "the read decline is announced")
 389: row("rd sent", printed(t, "v0") if alive else "died", "0x0",
 390:     "declined READ reaches the tail and returns a DEFINED 0, not the sentinel")
 391: 
 392: A = Addr(CODE)
 393: t, alive, how = session(load(A, RE + UNMAP_R) + ["print v0"])
 394: row("rd nodbe", ("exception" in t.lower()) or ("DBE" in t), False,
 395:     "a decline is not a guest bus error -- kills `return 0'")
 396: 
 397: # ----------------------------------- L2 REPAIR: the WIDTH axis, and the FIRST component
 398: #  *** ADDED 2026-08-31 AFTER THE PASS-2 SEAT MEASURED TWO MUTANTS SWEEPING ALL 28 ROWS
 399: #  CLEAN, ONE OF THEM A VERBATIM REINSTATEMENT OF THE REMOVED KILL. ***
 400: #
 401: #  The 28 rows above pin the DIRECTION axis exhaustively -- write, read, per-direction
 402: #  latches, the sentinel, the DBE -- and never touch the WIDTH axis at the catch-all,
 403: #  because store() defaults to OP_SD and load() to OP_LD.  Every catch-all row was len 8.
 404: #  The round's HEADLINE is `no width predicate at all' and its WITNESS is a `lb', so the
 405: #  one axis the fix is about was the one axis the detector could not see.  Mutant `W' --
 406: #  re-adding the pre-#499 `len != 8' kill, lifted verbatim from 9f666a8^ -- scored 28/28
 407: #  while `sb' and `lb' at 0xb5001800 died with the pre-fix text.  Floor clause (b).
 408: #
 409: #  Second blindness, same cause one level up: the catch-all has TWO disjoint components,
 410: #  0x16e0-0x16ff (32 bytes, and it is CRIME_RE_CLIP_IDS -- a NAMED register block the
 411: #  model has not implemented, not anonymous space) and 0x1800-0x1fff (2048).  All four
 412: #  UNMAP_* offsets are 0x800/0x8c0/0x900/0x9c0 -- the second component.  THE 32-BYTE
 413: #  COMPONENT HAD ZERO ROWS, so `T' (CRIME_RE_TEX + 0xe0 -> + 0x100, one hex digit) handed
 414: #  it back to exit(1) and scored 28/28.  Clause (d): a bound relaxed on a dominating
 415: #  predicate.
 416: A = Addr(CODE)
 417: t, alive, how = session(store(A, RE + UNMAP_W, op=OP_SB_T0_A3, val="0x5a"))
 418: row("wr narrow surv", how, "exit0",
 419:     "a BYTE write to the catch-all survives -- kills a re-added len guard")
 420: row("wr narrow decl", t.count(wr_decl(UNMAP_W, datum("0x5a"))), 1,
 421:     "...and is announced: the decline is width-agnostic, as the fix claims")
 422: 
 423: A = Addr(CODE)
 424: t, alive, how = session(load(A, RE + UNMAP_R, op=OP_LW_V0_AT) + ["print v0"])
 425: row("rd narrow surv", how, "exit0",
 426:     "a 4-byte READ of the catch-all survives -- the witness width, not just len 8")
 427: row("rd narrow sent", printed(t, "v0") if alive else "died", "0x0",
 428:     "...and still lands a DEFINED 0 rather than the sentinel")
 429: 
 430: #  CLIP_IDS: the FIRST component.  0x6e0 + the handler's own +0x1000 = 0x16e0.
 431: A = Addr(CODE)
 432: t, alive, how = session(store(A, RE + 0x6e0))
 433: row("clip surv", how, "exit0",
 434:     "comp1 base, len8, WRITE survives (killed by the pre-fix build)")
 435: row("clip decl", t.count(wr_decl(0x6e0)), 1,
 436:     "...and is announced, so the component is covered rather than merely alive")
 437: 
 438: #  *** AND THE SAME AXIS AGAIN, ONE LEVEL DOWN.  Added 2026-08-31 after two packet-fed
 439: #  seats read the repair above and pointed out that its own claim -- `the WIDTH axis is
 440: #  pinned' -- covers only TWO CELLS of a two-by-two.  The rows above pin
 441: #  component2-x-narrow and component2-x-len8 and component1-x-len8; component1 was left
 442: #  at store()'s default OP_SD, so COMPONENT-1-x-NARROW had nothing.
 443: #
 444: #  That is the ORIGINAL breach reproduced inside its own repair: I diagnosed `one axis
 445: #  pinned exhaustively, the other not at all', fixed it at the address the mutants used,
 446: #  and left the identical hole at the other component.  A guard re-added at the catch-all
 447: #  would be caught here; a guard re-added and CONDITIONED on the first component would
 448: #  not have been.
 449: A = Addr(CODE)
 450: t, alive, how = session(store(A, RE + 0x6e0, op=OP_SB_T0_A3, val="0x5a"))
 451: row("clip nar surv", how, "exit0",
