 254:                 one pcc_timer_tick callback increments both counts and reassert_interrupts reads
 255:                 both, so (p1, p2) is a joint input of the model.  EIGHT floor cells, every one held
 256:                 at a wide write: (T2, 0, 0) by `latch all' (0x0003) and `rb t2icr' (0xaab8), (T1, 0, 0) by `op t1icr dcl' (0x0303) and `rb t1icr' -- NOT `latch all', which iterates BLOCKS12 at 0x1a and never writes T1ICR (Opus, pass 11); (T1, >0, 0) `pend1 rb'; (T2, >0,
 257:                 0) `pend1 rb2'; (T2, 0, >0) `pend2 rb'; (T1, 0, >0) `pend2 rb1'; (T2, >0, >0)
 258:                 `pendboth rb'; (T1, >0, >0) `pendboth rb1'.  PLUS TWO, pass 13 -- the INT axis, which the
 259:                 pass-11 enumeration dismissed as derived from the count: an IEN-clear byte write zeroes
 260:                 the count and leaves INT set (the body clears INT only on ICLR; reassert only sets it),
 261:                 so (label, INT set, own count 0) is a reachable joint state of two body-read device
 262:                 lvalues -- held by `pend2 zctl/rbz' and `pend1 zctl/rbz' (the control readback 0x23 is
 263:                 the cell's signature), killed by `&& !((reg & INT) && p == 0 && label)'.  TEN cells.
 264:                 BEYOND THE FLOOR, HELD AS A GENERATING
 265:                 SET (grok, pass 11): the bits of the written idata that the body tests -- IEN (0x10),
 266:                 ICLR (0x08, a write strobe), the HUH? bits 0xe0 -- are single-operand MARGINALS of
 267:                 the value, not floor; yet at EVERY pending cell each is written both clear and set
 268:                 (0x0000; 0x0013; 0x0018; 0x0020 -- the `*i', `*c', `*h' readbacks, with a `huh' row
 269:                 per session as the HUH? print channel), so any single-axis extra conjunct on one of
 270:                 them at a pending cell lands a write and reds a readback (M_P2IEN, M_ICLR, M_HI,
 271:                 M_P1IEN).  The idle rows drive 0xaab8 (IEN|ICLR|INT|0x80) at both labels and 0x0003 / 0x0303, so the same
 272:                 holds at the (0, 0) cells.  DISCLOSED, with the derivation: multi-axis idata joints at
 273:                 a pending cell (`!(p2 && (idata & ICLR) && (idata & 0xe0))' and the like -- every held
 274:                 write sets one tested bit beyond IEN, except 0x0018, which sets IEN AND ICLR -- 'at most
 275:                 one of the three' until pass 13); INT clear with a count pending -- NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE BY
 276:                 A PROBE and DISCLOSED, not 'unreachable' as this said until pass 13: pcc_timer_tick()
 277:                 increments the count from the host timer WITHOUT calling reassert_interrupts(), INT is
 278:                 set at the next DEVICE_TICK, so the cell exists in that window (GPT-6 Astra; grok's
 279:                 'reassert sets INT before any guard runs' was wrong); pending counts >= 2 at once (the body tests `> 0' only; grok read OpenBSD's
 280:                 clock.c as arming COC on both timers -- not in this tree, NOT independently verified;
 281:                 the in-tree warrant is the model's joint handling); `idata == k' for any k no row
 282:                 drives; TxICR 0x37; TxCTL 0xff; the overflow count at 2-7 and 9-15.  Pass 9 held one
 283:                 floor cell; pass 10 the label mirror and its neighbours (Opus, codex); pass 11 found
 284:                 the ICLR x pending cell open (three seats, the Opus seat measured it) and the rule's
 285:                 letter over-demanding (its own author).  The De Morgan form of the original gap (kimi
 286:                 substitute): `!(p1 && p2)' is `p1 == 0 || p2 == 0' -- neither disjunct true of all its
 287:                 lvalue's held values, the disjunction true in every row, so a per-lvalue disclosure
 288:                 test could never fire on it.
 289:                 THE ENUMERATION ACROSS THE ARMS (pass 11 batch two; the class-closure amendment: three
 290:                 passes found one class -- an unvaried axis crossed with a varied one -- so the repair
 291:                 owes the enumeration, not another cell).  Read off each guarded write body, the axes its
 292:                 code makes DECISIVE (tested in an `if', or used as an index), and what the rows hold:
 293:                   GENCTL, SCCERR, PSCALEADJ, MASK -- stores or a print with NO `if' on state or idata:
 294:                      no axis beyond the label; the plain rows hold every label.  (Their callee
 295:                      reassert_interrupts tests C040/MIEN -- out of the closure: non-transitive.)
 296:                   VECBASE, SCCICR, SCCTX, SCCRX, SCSIICR -- each tests ONE idata partition, its HUH?
 297:                      bits (`idata & ~0xf0' / `~0x1f' / `~0x1f' / `~0xdf' / `~0xdf', on the COMPOSED
 298:                      idata).  HUH?-SET is held by every wide row at them (0x0303, 0xaab8 and the
 299:                      rb4/rb8 lanes all carry bits outside the mask); HUH?-CLEAR by the pass-13 `rbq'
 300:                      rows (0x00f0 / 0x0010 / 0x0010 / 0x0001 / 0x0001), killed by `&& (idata & ~mask)'
 301:                      at each arm -- AND by the `latch all*' announce-count rows, which write 0x0000 /
 302:                      0x0001 / 0x0003 at every block and so already held HUH?-clear here (part 13:
 303:                      M_HUHV 249/251, the four others 244/251, each red on `rbq' plus the latch rows).
 304:                      The `rbq' rows add the LANDING channel (the stored masked value); the cells were
 305:                      not open.  *This enumeration listed all five among the no-`if' arms until pass 13
 306:                      (GPT-6 Astra fix review): five conditional HUH? prints; the pass first called them
 307:                      five open cells and the table refuted that.*
 308:                   IPL -- one function-static latch `w': held clear (`ipl noig2') and set (`ipl wset').
 309:                   TxCTL -- the label (an RMW index), the register's overflow-count class {0, 1, >= 8,
 310:                      0xfc-via-memcpy} and two tested idata bits, COVF (`if (idata & PCC2_TCTL_COVF)')
 311:                      and the HUH? bits (`if (idata & ~7)' -- on the COMPOSED idata, not the lane: a
 312:                      halfword 0x0303 counts, which is how `M_TXHIOVF' landed the b27 rows' writes).
 313:                      COVF-set was held only at the plain cell (the rb4/rb8 lanes 0xdd and 0x44 carry
 314:                      bit 2; batch two first said 'at no cell'), never at a COUNT cell.  Generating set:
 315:                      in the four overflow
 316:                      sessions COVF-set (0x0004) and HUH?-bit-set (0x0008) writes at the ARMED label,
 317:                      then the IDLE label preset to 0x02 (COC without CEN) with 0x0000 / 0x0004 /
 318:                      0x0008 -- the `ovf* rbv/rbx/rb1/rb1v/rb1x' and `ovf1/ovfhi1 rb2*' readbacks and an
 319:                      `ovf* huh' row per session.  Landed values never equal a preset: count 1 -> 0x00
 320:                      (COVF clears the count and itself) / 0x10 (+ HUH?); count >= 8 -> 0x00 / 0x80
 321:                      masked; idle 0x02 -> 0x00.  Disclosed: COVF at the 0xfc cell (rests on the filed
 322:                      pcc2counter8 path) and at the plain 0x03 cell (a preset of 0x03 would start the
 323:                      idle timer); the HUH? bits are held at the plain cell by 0xaab8 (lane 0xb8).
 324:                   TxICR -- passes 9 to 11 above.
 325:                 A future arm added to the guard set owes this paragraph one line before its rows.
 326:                 Bit 3 (ICLR, 0x08) is a WRITE STROBE: the body TESTS it (`idata & PCC2_TTIRQ_ICLR') and
 327:                 never stores it -- the store mask 0x17 is bits 0, 1, 2, 4 -- so the register bit is set by
 328:                 no writer (pass 10 accepted a sentence calling the mask a writer of it; pass 11 reverted
 329:                 that: 0x17 & 0x08 == 0).  Bits 6-7 of the TxICR byte are set by no writer at all (body `idata & 0x17',
 330:                 reassert bit 5, the counter memcpy cannot reach 0x1a): E, same warrant.
 331:         IPL     reads the function-static `w' of its WRITE branch (its #119 print latch):
 332:                 `ipl wset'.  The READ branch has a second static of the same name; it is
 333:                 outside the closure (not the guarded write body) and `ipl rset' holds it
 334:                 set anyway.
 335:         helper  reads d->warned: `rb2 *' holds each arm's OWN bit set; a guard naming
 336:                 ANOTHER arm's bit (the sibling round's foreign-bit cell, sgi_de pass 16,
 337:                 filed there as derived-not-measured) is held by `latch all' + `latch all
 338:                 rev' -- every ordered pair of blocks, measured in part 8.
 339:         GENCTL, VECBASE, SCCICR, SCCTX, SCCRX, SCSIICR, MASK: pure stores (`= idata & m'),
 340:                 reading no PRIOR device state -- `idata' (the value under test, read by ten
 341:                 of the twelve bodies) is held by every wide-write row and pinned per arm by
 342:                 `latch all' / `latch all one' / `latch all zero'.  SCCERR: constant store.
 343:                 PSCALEADJ: reads only idata (print).  So a guard conditioned on those registers' bits
 344:                 (the SCC* INT bits included) is OUTSIDE the closure; the byte presets still
 345:                 pin their landing.
 346:       OUT OF CLOSURE, disclosed not owed: d->pcctwo_reg[PCCTWO_IPL] is read by the IPL arm's
 347:       READ branch and by the callee reassert_interrupts(), not by IPL's guarded write body --
 348:       `&& reg[IPL] == 0' at the IPL guard escapes with a one-message consequence, and at any
 349:       arm no row wide-writes with an interrupt pending; at TxICR the pend rows DO (reassert
 350:       has raised IPL to the pending level), so the all-twelve form is killed there: MEASURED
 351:       by the pass-7 Opus seat, 155/159, red pend1/pend2 decl+rb (pass7_seats_20260904/opus/).
 352:       Likewise `&& pending_timer2 == 0' at all twelve: 157/159,
 353:       the TxICR-only signature -- the conjunct is invisible at the other eleven arms, which
 354:       is what the non-transitive closure predicts and discloses;
 355:       cur_int_vec[] is WRITTEN by reassert_interrupts() and read only by the IACK handler.
 356:       GATE 14 IS LOAD-SENSITIVE since pass 6: the pend*/ovf* rows need the host's 100 Hz
 357:       SIGALRM to fire during a `continue' (20 s ceiling -- inert until pass 8: the tuple's
 358:       third element was read after unpacking, so the wait returned at once), so a starved
 359:       host reds them for a
 360:       reason the row names (`no-breakpoint') -- run the gate alone.  Their poll loops also
 361:       rely on GENCTL.MIEN being clear at init, so the guest never takes the interrupt.
 362:       At GENCTL the 4-/8-byte lanes are 0xd9 / 0x40: 0xdd and 0x44 carry PCC2_C040 and a
 363:       LANDED write there ends the host (pcc2c040kill) -- the row would still kill, by death
 364:       instead of by value, and the NOROW line below would be false (pass 7, measured).
 365:       reassert_interrupts() (a callee of seven bodies) reads GENCTL, the pending counts, the
 366:       TxICR / SCC* IEN, INT and IL bits, MASK and IPL.  `latch all fail' rests on memory_rw's
 367:       debug() line, which prints because this probe single-steps.
 368:       pending_timer1/2_interrupts are INCREMENTED only by pcc_timer_tick (a SIGALRM callback
 369:       that debugger.c stops during `step'); the TxICR body clears and decrements them.
 370:       NOT PINNED, disclosed: the announce's `len=%i' value -- no row reads it (cosmetic,
 371:       the NAME gap's sibling).  And the generic-DECL counts are over the WHOLE pty
 372:       transcript: three other devices emit the same suffix, none instantiated on mvme187.
 373:       OTHER DEVICE STATE AS A GUARD OPERAND (pass 6).  A guard conditioned on
 374:       d->pcctwo_reg[], pending_timer*, the TxICR INT bit or reg[IPL] being NONZERO
 375:       declines nothing in the init-state sessions (of the twelve guarded registers only
 376:       VECBASE 0x0f and PSCALEADJ 0xdf are non-zero at init; CHIPID 0x20 is, and is not one
 377:       of them), so `latch all' reads 0 -- killed.  One conditioned on them
 378:       being ZERO is the shipped behaviour in every row that holds the field at its init
 379:       value; MEASURED by both Agent seats at TxICR (`&& !d->pending_timer2_interrupts',
 380:       `&& d->pending_timer1_interrupts == 0': 118/118 each) and closed as a class -- see
 381:       THE GUARD'S OPERAND SPACE below.  The latch-set check (`rb2 *') is at width 2 only;
 382:       the qualified-guard shape is width-agnostic, so its 4- and 8-byte repeats are
 383:       coverage debt, FILED, not a floor cell.
 384:       THE ODD BLOCKS FIRST.  Every guest-side channel at an odd block is absent by
 385:       construction, and three consecutive passes found a shape with no channel there
 386:       (fall-through x4, then at VECBASE and IPL, then FAULT x6).  A new shape is checked
 387:       against the six operator-only blocks before anything else.
 388:       INSTRUMENTS.  Parts 3, 3b and 3c ran three frozen copies (md5 3dcf73de, 280d9ab3,
 389:       72759b4f); the last is the shipped probe.  3 -> 3b changed only `rb t1ctl' /
 390:       `rb t1icr's expected string, 3b -> 3c only `acc all's session; row-name sets are
 391:       identical and no killing row was touched, so the part-3 kills TRANSFER.  `acc all'
 392:       was REWRITTEN, not added: its warrant is that the session is self-contained and
 393:       part 3c measured the rewrite (95/96, `acc all' alone).
 394: 
 395:   DOES NOT CATCH, stated so an escape is outside the contract rather than an argument
 396:     * per-instance vs process-global latch state: mvme187 instantiates ONE pcc2, so no
 397:       session can hold two instances.  The bitfield is per-instance by construction;
 398:       nothing here measures it;
 399:     * pcc2c040kill -- a LEGAL byte write of 0x04 to GENCTL still ends the host in
 400:       reassert_interrupts().  Every GENCTL lane value here keeps bit 0x04 CLEAR so no
 401:       row dies for that reason;
 402:     * pcc2defaultkill -- FIXED by #501: an unlisted offset (0x06, 0x14, 0x18, 0x2c ...) no
 403:       longer ends the host in `default:'; regress/pcc2_default_probe.py (46 rows) pins it, and
 404:       nothing HERE measures that arm (this line said "still ends" until #501's pass 4);
 405:     * pcc2counter8 -- the counter arm's raw memcpy of an 8-byte write;
 406:     * what real hardware does with the LANES of a wide write (not on disk);
 407:     * the SCCERR word-write's stored value: the arm always stores 0, so a decline and
 408:       an accept are value-identical there and the row's channel is the message.
 409: 
 410: Sentinel: PCC2W_PROBE_DONE
 411: """
 412: 
 413: import os, pty, re, select, sys, time
 414: 
 415: BIN = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "build/gxemul"
 416: LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "local"
 417: 
 418: DUMMY = "/tmp/pcc2_dummy.bin"
 419: open(DUMMY, "wb").write(b"\x00\x00\x00\x00")
 420: 
 421: CODE = 0x00010000
 422: SCRATCH = 0x00020000
 423: PCC2 = 0xfff42000
 424: #  the SIX GUEST-reachable blocks (even offsets; IPL below is the sixth) and the six
 425: #  OPERATOR-only ones (odd offsets; T1CTL/T1ICR are odd labels of the shared TxCTL/TxICR
 426: #  blocks).  An earlier comment here said five and seven: a units slip, blocks vs labels.
 427: GENCTL, T2CTL, T2ICR, SCCERR, SCCTX = 0x02, 0x16, 0x1a, 0x1c, 0x1e
 428: VECBASE, PSCALEADJ, T1CTL, T1ICR, SCCICR, SCCRX, SCSIICR = 0x03, 0x15, 0x17, 0x1b, 0x1d, 0x1f, 0x2f
 429: #  pcc2 pass 2: THE TWO FOLDED-IN ARMS HAD NO ROW AT ALL.  A seat found that the probe
 430: #  touched no offset at 0x3e or 0x3f -- twelve blocks converted, ten given rows.  MASK
 431: #  is GENCTL's byte-identical twin (store byte, reassert); GENCTL's null-repair was
 432: #  caught by `rb genctl', MASK's by nothing, a 60/60 sweep.  AND IPL IS EVEN: it is the
 433: #  SIXTH guest-reachable block, not a seventh operator one.
 434: IPL, MASK = 0x3e, 0x3f
 435: CHIPID = 0x00
 436: 
 437: 
 438: def enc(op26, rd, rs1, imm):
 439:     return (op26 << 26) | (rd << 21) | (rs1 << 16) | (imm & 0xffff)
 440: 
 441: 
 442: #  r2 = PCC2 base, r3 = scratch, r4 = load target, r5 = store source, r6 = second source
 443: #  ld.b / ld.h (0x07 / 0x06) SIGN-EXTEND: 0x82 would print as 0xffffff82.  Every row that
 444: #  asserts a VALUE uses the unsigned forms ld.bu / ld.hu (0x03 / 0x02); the survival rows
 445: #  only check exit status and keep the signed forms.
 446: def LD_B(rd, off): return enc(0x07, rd, 2, off)
 447: def LD_H(rd, off): return enc(0x06, rd, 2, off)
 448: def LD_BU(rd, off): return enc(0x03, rd, 2, off)
 449: def LD_HU(rd, off): return enc(0x02, rd, 2, off)
 450: def LD_W(rd, off): return enc(0x05, rd, 2, off)
 451: def ST_B(rs, off): return enc(0x0b, rs, 2, off)
 452: def ST_H(rs, off): return enc(0x0a, rs, 2, off)
 453: def ST_W(rs, off): return enc(0x09, rs, 2, off)
 454: I_ST_SCR = enc(0x09, 5, 3, 0)          # st  r5,r3,0   scratch word
 455: I_LD_SCR = enc(0x05, 4, 3, 0)          # ld  r4,r3,0
 456: I_BR_SELF = 0xc0000000
 457: 
 458: SENTINEL = 0xdeadbeef
 459: DEVSIG = "IGNORING write to read-only PCCTWO_CHIPID"
 460: DECL = "-- declined.  (once) ]"
 461: rows = []
 462: 
 463: 
 464: def row(name, got, want, note=""):
 465:     assert name not in [n for n, _ in rows], "DUPLICATE ROW NAME %r" % name
 466:     assert len(name) <= 15, name    # load-bearing for gate_arm.sh: `%-16s' plus a literal space keep its `^$v  .*ok$' pattern satisfiable (pass 9, Opus)
 467:     ok = (got == want)
 468:     rows.append((name, ok))
 469:     print("%-16s %-12s %-12s %-46s %s" % (name, str(got), str(want), note,
 470:                                           "ok" if ok else "FAIL"))
 471:     return ok
 472: 
 473: 
 474: def session(cmds, settle=1.5, spin=1.2):
 475:     pid, fd = pty.fork()
 476:     if pid == 0:
 477:         os.execv(BIN, [BIN, "-V", "-x", "-E", "mvme88k", "-e", "mvme187", "-M", "64",
 478:                        "0x10000:" + DUMMY])
 479:         os._exit(127)
 480:     buf = ""
 481: 
 482:     def rd(t, until=None):
 483:         #  drain the pty for t seconds; with `until', return as soon as that text has
 484:         #  arrived (pass 7: a fixed drain after `continue' could send the next command to a
 485:         #  guest that had not reached its breakpoint yet).
 486:         nonlocal buf
 487:         end = time.time() + t
 488:         while time.time() < end:
 489:             if until is not None and until in buf:
 490:                 return True
 491:             r, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0.1)
 492:             if not r:
 493:                 continue
 494:             try:
 495:                 d = os.read(fd, 65536)
 496:                 if not d:
 497:                     return False
 498:                 buf += d.decode("latin-1", "replace")
 499:             except OSError:
 500:                 return False
 501:         if until is not None and until in buf:    # pass 9 (codex): the token may land in the last read
 502:             return True
 503:         return "timeout" if until is not None else True
 504: 
 505:     alive = rd(settle)
 506:     how = "nostatus"
 507:     for i, c in enumerate(cmds):
 508:         w = spin if i == len(cmds) - 1 else 0.25
 509:         until = None
 510:         if isinstance(c, tuple):    # (cmd, wait[, until]): `continue' waits for its breakpoint
 511:             until = c[2] if len(c) > 2 else None    # read the tuple BEFORE unpacking it
 512:             c, w = c[0], c[1]
 513:         try:
 514:             #  the one unbounded call left (pass 9, Opus): it blocks only if the pty input buffer fills
 515:             #  while the guest free-runs -- tens of bytes per command against a kilobyte buffer.
 516:             os.write(fd, (c + "\n").encode("latin-1"))
 517:         except OSError:
 518:             alive = False
 519:             break
 520:         r = rd(w, until)
 521:         if r is False:
 522:             alive = False
 523:             break
 524:         if r == "timeout":
 525:             #  pass 8 (codex, grok): the guest never reached its breakpoint -- send it nothing
 526:             #  more, and let every row of this session say so through cval().
 527:             how = "no-breakpoint"
 528:             break
 529:     try:
 530:         os.write(fd, b"quit\n")
 531:         rd(0.4)
 532:     except OSError:
 533:         pass
 534:     try:
 535:         os.close(fd)
 536:     except OSError:
 537:         pass
 538:     how = how if how == "no-breakpoint" else "nostatus"
 539:     #  pass 7: a guest still running (no breakpoint reached) would block waitpid forever;
 540:     #  give it a moment after the pty closed, then kill it -- the row says so, the gate
 541:     #  does not hang.
 542:     stat = None
 543:     reaped = False
 544:     for _ in range(30):
 545:         try:
 546:             p, stat = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)
 547:         except OSError:
 548:             p, stat = pid, None
 549:         if p:
 550:             reaped = True
 551:             break
 552:         time.sleep(0.1)
 553:     if not reaped:
 554:         try:
 555:             os.kill(pid, 9)
 556:         except OSError:
 557:             pass
 558:         how = how if how == "no-breakpoint" else "killed"
 559:         for _ in range(30):    # pass 8 (Opus F2): reap the killed child, bounded
 560:             try:
 561:                 p, stat = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)
 562:             except OSError:
 563:                 p, stat = pid, None
 564:             if p:
 565:                 reaped = True
 566:                 break
 567:             time.sleep(0.1)
 568:         if not reaped:
 569:             how = how if how == "no-breakpoint" else "unreaped"
 570:     try:
 571:         if stat is None or not reaped or how in ("no-breakpoint", "unreaped", "killed"):
 572:             pass
 573:         elif os.WIFSIGNALED(stat):
 574:             how = "sig%d" % os.WTERMSIG(stat)
 575:         elif os.WIFEXITED(stat):
 576:             how = "exit%d" % os.WEXITSTATUS(stat)
 577:     except OSError:
 578:         pass
 579:     return buf.replace("\r", ""), alive, how
 580: 
 581: 
 582: def printed(t, reg):
 583:     m = re.search(r"print\s+%s\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)" % reg, t)
 584:     return "0x%x" % int(m.group(1), 16) if m else "absent"
 585: 
 586: 
 587: def program(insns, at=CODE):
 588:     #  `at' lets a session run TWO programs: a second sequence at the SAME address finds
 589:     #  pc already there and the assignment is skipped (the Addr hazard, designed out in
 590:     #  the sgi probes with Addr.take()).  Callers needing two pass at=CODE + 0x100.
 591:     words = list(insns) + [I_BR_SELF, 0]
 592:     cmds = ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * i, w) for i, w in enumerate(words)]
 593:     return cmds + ["pc=0x%x" % at, "step %d" % len(insns)]
 594: 
 595: 
 596: def setup(r5="0x5a5a5a5a", r6="0x0"):
 597:     return ["r2=0x%x" % PCC2, "r3=0x%x" % SCRATCH, "r5=%s" % r5, "r6=%s" % r6,
 598:             "r4=0x%x" % SENTINEL]
 599: 
 600: 
 601: print("pcc2widthkills DETECTOR -- binary=%s label=%s" % (BIN, LABEL))
 602: print("%-16s %-12s %-12s %-46s %s" % ("row", "got", "want", "note", ""))
 603: 
 604: # ------------------------------------------------------------------ controls
 605: t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([I_ST_SCR, I_LD_SCR]) + ["print r4"])
 606: row("live", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x5a5a5a5a",
 607:     "RAM word round-trips through the same decode")
 608: t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([ST_B(5, CHIPID)]))
 609: row("devsig", t.count(DEVSIG), 1, "a byte write to CHIPID makes the DEVICE speak")
 610: t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([I_ST_SCR, LD_B(4, GENCTL), I_LD_SCR]) + ["print r4"])
 611: row("byte rd", how, "exit0", "ld.b GENCTL: the legal width, serviced on both builds")
 612: row("byte rd liv", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x5a5a5a5a", "...and runs on")
 613: 
 614: # --------------------------------------- survival pairs at the five reachable blocks
 615: #  Each kill row is PAIRED with a positive post-access observable.
 616: for nm, off in (("genctl", GENCTL), ("t2ctl", T2CTL), ("t2icr", T2ICR),
 617:                 ("sccerr", SCCERR), ("scctx", SCCTX)):
 618:     t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([I_ST_SCR, LD_H(4, off), I_LD_SCR]) + ["print r4"])
 619:     row("hrd " + nm, how, "exit0", "ld.h %s (aligned halfword READ) survives" % nm.upper())
 620:     row("hrd %s lv" % nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x5a5a5a5a", "...and runs on")
 621:     row("hrd %s nod" % nm, t.count(DECL), 0,
 622:         "...and a wide READ is never declined (the direction split's own conjunct)")
 623:     #  r6 = the halfword to store: both lanes keep GENCTL's bit 0x04 CLEAR (pcc2c040kill)
 624:     t, alive, how = session(setup(r6="0xaabb") + program([I_ST_SCR, ST_H(6, off), I_LD_SCR]) + ["print r4"])
 625:     row("hwr " + nm, how, "exit0", "st.h %s (aligned halfword WRITE) survives" % nm.upper())
 626:     row("hwr %s lv" % nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x5a5a5a5a", "...and runs on")
 627: #  SCCERR is the one 4-aligned block: word read AND write
 628: t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([I_ST_SCR, LD_W(4, SCCERR), I_LD_SCR]) + ["print r4"])
 629: row("wrd sccerr", how, "exit0", "ld SCCERR (the one 4-aligned block) survives")
 630: row("wrd sccerr lv", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x5a5a5a5a", "...and runs on")
 631: row("wrd sccerr nod", t.count(DECL), 0, "...and the word READ is never declined")
 632: t, alive, how = session(setup(r6="0x00000000") + program([I_ST_SCR, ST_W(6, SCCERR), I_LD_SCR]) + ["print r4"])
 633: row("wwr sccerr", how, "exit0", "st SCCERR (word WRITE) survives")
 634: row("wwr sccerr lv", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x5a5a5a5a", "...and runs on")
 635: #  SCCERR's arm always stores 0, so decline and accept are VALUE-identical there: the
 636: #  only channel that varies is the announcement.
 637: row("wwr sccerr dcl", t.count("write to PCCTWO_SCCERR " + DECL), 1,
 638:     "...and it was DECLINED once -- the message is the only channel here")
 639: 
 640: # ---------------------------------------------------------- VALUE rows (reads)
 641: #  A wide read must compose the lanes in ADDRESS order.  VECBASE's arm masks & 0xf0
 642: #  and GENCTL's stores the byte, so the halfword at 0x02 is GENCTL<<8 | VECBASE.
 643: #  0x82 keeps bit 0x04 clear.
 644: t, alive, how = session(setup(r5="0x82", r6="0x50")
 645:                         + program([ST_B(5, GENCTL), ST_B(6, VECBASE), LD_HU(4, GENCTL)]) + ["print r4"])
 646: row("val h genctl", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x8250",
 647:     "ld.h at GENCTL composes GENCTL:VECBASE in address order -- kills lane-order / zero-fill")
 648: #  word at SCCERR: SCCERR always 0; SCCICR & 0x1f; SCCTX & 0x1f; SCCRX & 0xdf.
 649: t, alive, how = session(setup(r5="0x15", r6="0x1f")
 650:                         + program([ST_B(5, SCCICR), ST_B(6, SCCTX), ST_B(6, SCCRX), LD_W(4, SCCERR)]) + ["print r4"])
 651: row("val w sccerr", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x151f1f",
 652:     "ld at SCCERR composes 00:SCCICR:SCCTX:SCCRX -- four lanes, right order")
 653: 
 654: # ------------------------------------------------ READBACK rows (the DELETE killer)
 655: #  After a declined st.h 0xAABB to GENCTL, BOTH lanes must be unchanged.  Under a bare
 656: #  deletion GENCTL reads 0xBB (the neighbour's lane); under an accidental compose it
 657: #  reads 0xAA and VECBASE 0xB0.  Both lanes of 0xAABB keep bit 0x04 clear.
 658: t, alive, how = session(setup(r5="0x82", r6="0xaabb")
 659:                         + program([ST_B(5, GENCTL), ST_H(6, GENCTL), LD_BU(4, GENCTL)]) + ["print r4"])
 660: row("rb genctl", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x82",
 661:     "GENCTL unchanged after a declined st.h -- kills DELETE (0xbb) and compose (0xaa)")
 662: row("rb genctl dcl", t.count("write to PCCTWO_GENCTL " + DECL), 1,
 663:     "...and the decline was announced ONCE")
 664: t, alive, how = session(setup(r5="0x50", r6="0xaabb")
 665:                         + program([ST_B(5, VECBASE), ST_H(6, GENCTL), LD_BU(4, VECBASE)]) + ["print r4"])
 666: row("rb vecbase", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x50",
 667:     "VECBASE unchanged too -- the second lane of the declined halfword")
 668: 
 669: # ---------------------------- per-arm channels (pass 2: sibling parity, arm by arm)
 670: #  A seat pointed out that only GENCTL had a readback: every other reachable arm's
 671: #  halfword-write row checked SURVIVAL alone, so a guard edited at ONE arm (`len > 2',
 672: #  or the guard deleted, at T2ICR only) left every row green.  Each arm now has its own
 673: #  channel, with a lane value its own mask turns into a different byte when it lands.
 674: for nm, off, pre, landed in (("t2ctl", T2CTL, "0x03", "0x3"), ("t2icr", T2ICR, "0x13", "0x13"),
 675:                              ("scctx", SCCTX, "0x1f", "0x1f")):
 676:     t, alive, how = session(setup(r5=pre, r6="0xaab8")
 677:                             + program([ST_B(5, off), ST_H(6, off), LD_BU(4, off)]) + ["print r4"])
 678:     row("rb " + nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", landed,
 679:         "%s unchanged after a declined st.h -- kills a guard edited at THIS arm" % nm.upper())
 680:     row("rb %s dcl" % nm, t.count("write to PCCTWO_%s " % ("TxCTL" if nm == "t2ctl" else "TxICR" if nm == "t2icr" else "SCCTX") + DECL), 1,
 681:         "...announced once at this arm")
 682: t, alive, how = session(setup(r6="0xaab8") + program([ST_H(6, SCCERR)]))
 683: row("hwr sccerr dcl", t.count("write to PCCTWO_SCCERR " + DECL), 1,
 684:     "halfword write to SCCERR declined once -- value-identical arm, message channel")
 685: 
 686: #  PRE-TABLE BLOCK yield (section 1, guard field vs body field): the guard reads the access
 687: #  SHAPE (len) and the guarded body reads the VALUE (idata).  An operand swap to a value
 688: #  test -- `idata > 0xff', a plausible "does it fit a byte" reading -- accepts a halfword
 689: #  write whose value fits, and big-endian 0x0022 then stores 0x22, the NEIGHBOUR's lane,
 690: #  into GENCTL: the original defect, behind a guard that still reads like a width check.
 691: #  Every other wide-write row used a value above 0xff, so all 77 were green under it BY
 692: #  CONSTRUCTION.  Written before the repair table ran; the table says whether it kills.
 693: t, alive, how = session(setup(r5="0x11", r6="0x0022")
 694:                         + program([ST_B(5, GENCTL), ST_H(6, GENCTL), LD_BU(4, GENCTL)]) + ["print r4"])
 695: row("rb genctl lo", printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", "0x11",
 696:     "st.h of a value that FITS a byte is still declined -- the guard is on len, not idata")
 697: 
 698: # ------------------------- latch CARDINALITY (pass 2, the measuring seat's class closer)
 699: #  `latch same' and `latch two' pin ONE pair out of 66: every other session writes at most
 700: #  one BLOCK, so a bit shared by any other pair announces normally and no row moves.
 701: #  MEASURED by the builder: aliasing SCCTX onto SCCRX's bit -- a ONE-CHARACTER edit --
 702: #  left the 60-row detector at 60/60.  ONE OFFSET PER BLOCK: TxCTL serves T1CTL+T2CTL
 703: #  and TxICR serves T1ICR+T2ICR, so twelve LABELS would give only ten announces -- the
 704: #  same units slip that let "five even blocks + seven odd ones = twelve" read as all
 705: #  twelve blocks.  This row pins the CARDINALITY of the latch: any collision anywhere in
 706: #  the 12-bit space drops the count.  (Operator path for all twelve, so the odd ones are
 707: #  reachable; the guest-reachable halves have their own rows above.)
 708: BLOCKS12 = (("GENCTL", 0x02), ("VECBASE", 0x03), ("PSCALEADJ", 0x15), ("TxCTL", 0x16),
 709:             ("TxICR", 0x1a), ("SCCERR", 0x1c), ("SCCICR", 0x1d), ("SCCTX", 0x1e),
 710:             ("SCCRX", 0x1f), ("SCSIICR", 0x2f), ("IPL", 0x3e), ("MASK", 0x3f))
 711: #  VALUE 0x0003, not 0x0303: it fits a byte, so this row ALSO reds if any arm swaps its
 712: #  guard operand from len to a value test (see `rb genctl lo').  On the fix the value
 713: #  never lands, so the expectation is value-independent.
 714: t, alive, how = session(["put h 0x%x, 0x0003" % (PCC2 + o) for _, o in BLOCKS12])
 715: row("latch all", t.count(DECL), 12,
 716:     "one wide write per BLOCK -> TWELVE announces: bit CARDINALITY, not one pair")
 717: row("latch all lv", how, "exit0", "...and the host survived all twelve blocks")
 718: #  PASS 5 (fable5, MEASURED): `break' -> `return 0' at an OPERATOR-only block is a total escape
 719: #  of the rows above -- the announce precedes the return, the body is skipped either way,
 720: #  and a failed debugger put does not threaten the host.  What the pty DOES carry is
 721: #  memory_rw's own line, "[ writing to device 'pcc2' addr ... failed ]", once per block
 722: #  whose guard returned 0.  Counted at ZERO over this session, it pins the FAULT member at
 723: #  all twelve blocks with no new session.  (At the six guest-reachable blocks the guest's
 724: #  own store faults and the hwr/lv pair reds as well -- part 4, M_RET0_GENCTL.)
 725: row("latch all fail", t.count("failed ]"), 0,
 726:     "twelve declined wide writes, ZERO device-write failures: DECLINE, not FAULT, at every block")
 727: 
 728: # ------------------------------------------------------------------ latch rows
 729: t, alive, how = session(setup(r6="0xaabb") + program([ST_H(6, GENCTL), ST_H(6, GENCTL)]))
 730: row("latch same", t.count("write to PCCTWO_GENCTL " + DECL), 1,
 731:     "same block twice -> ONE announce -- kills a dropped |= (flood)")
 732: t, alive, how = session(setup(r6="0x0303") + program([ST_H(6, GENCTL), ST_H(6, T2CTL)]))
 733: row("latch two", t.count(DECL), 2,
 734:     "two blocks -> TWO announces -- kills a bit shared across blocks")
 735: #  PASS 4 (glm, kimi, codex): `latch same' sees only CONSECUTIVE repeats, so `|=' -> `=' in the
 736: #  helper -- the field ASSIGNED instead of accumulated, one character -- passed every row: A
 737: #  then B clears A's bit, and nothing wrote A again afterwards.  Interleave: A, B, A -> TWO.
 738: t, alive, how = session(setup(r6="0x0303") + program([ST_H(6, GENCTL)])
 739:                         + ["put h 0x%x, 0x0303" % (PCC2 + VECBASE)]
 740:                         + program([ST_H(6, GENCTL)], at=CODE + 0x100))
 741: row("latch aba", t.count(DECL), 2,
 742:     "A, B, A -> TWO announces: the latch ACCUMULATES (an assignment would give three)")
 743: #  PASS 4 (minimax): `(1u << bit)' -> `1' in the SET line latches bit 0 for every block, so
 744: #  every block but GENCTL announces on every write.  `latch same' is at GENCTL (bit 0) and
 745: #  stays green.  The same test at a non-zero bit:
 746: t, alive, how = session(["put h 0x%x, 0x0303" % (PCC2 + MASK)] * 2)
 747: row("latch same2", t.count("write to PCCTWO_MASK " + DECL), 1,
 748:     "MASK (bit 11) twice -> ONE announce: the SET line names the block's own bit")
 749: 
 750: # ------------- PASS 5: the guard reading the FIX'S OWN STATE (MEASURED 101/101 by the Opus seat)
 751: #  `if (len != 1 && writeflag == MEM_WRITE && !(d->warned & (1u << bit)))' -- the canonical
 752: #  clause-(d) "condition qualified" form, at one arm or at all twelve -- swept every row above:
 753: #  the FIRST wide write is declined and announced exactly as before, and the SECOND lands the
 754: #  neighbour's lane.  `latch same' does two wide writes and reads only the count; every `rb'
 755: #  row reads back after exactly ONE.  No row ever observed the device at a decision point with
 756: #  its latch already set.  So, at every block: set a byte, write wide TWICE, then read back
 757: #  (or count the body's own print where the body stores nothing).  Even blocks by guest st.h,
 758: #  odd blocks by the operator's put h.  SCCERR stores 0 and is value-identical (E, disclosed).
 759: for nm, off, pre, want, guest in (("genctl", GENCTL, "0x82", "0x82", True), ("t2ctl", T2CTL, "0x03", "0x3", True),
 760:                                   ("t2icr", T2ICR, "0x13", "0x13", True), ("scctx", SCCTX, "0x1f", "0x1f", True),
 761:                                   ("vecbase", VECBASE, "0x50", "0x50", False), ("sccicr", SCCICR, "0x1f", "0x1f", False),
 762:                                   ("sccrx", SCCRX, "0x1f", "0x1f", False), ("scsiicr", SCSIICR, "0x1f", "0x1f", False),
 763:                                   ("mask", MASK, "0x12", "0x12", False)):
 764:     if guest:
 765:         t, alive, how = session(setup(r5=pre, r6="0xaab8") + program([ST_B(5, off), ST_H(6, off), ST_H(6, off), LD_BU(4, off)])
 766:                                 + ["print r4"])
 767:     else:
 768:         t, alive, how = session(setup(r5=pre) + program([ST_B(5, off)])
 769:                                 + ["put h 0x%x, 0xaab8" % (PCC2 + off)] * 2
 770:                                 + program([LD_BU(4, off)], at=CODE + 0x100) + ["print r4"])
 771:     row("rb2 " + nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", want,
 772:         "%s unchanged after TWO declined wide writes -- the second is refused with the latch SET" % nm.upper())
 773: t, alive, how = session(["put h 0x%x, 0x0303" % (PCC2 + PSCALEADJ)] * 2)
 774: row("pscale noig2", t.count("PSCALEADJ ignored"), 0,
 775:     "two declined wide writes never reach the 'ignored' print -- the second one would, unlatched")
 776: t, alive, how = session(setup(r6="0x0303") + program([ST_H(6, IPL), ST_H(6, IPL)]))
 777: row("ipl noig2", t.count("write to read-only PCCTWO_IPL"), 0,
 778:     "two declined st.h to IPL never reach the read-only print -- the second one would, unlatched")
 779: 
 780: #  And the wide READ that now falls through to each arm's SECOND predicate, `if (writeflag ==
 781: #  MEM_WRITE)' (the pre-fix guard killed reads before it was reached; the Opus seat flagged it).
 782: #  Delete that predicate at an even block and a wide READ stores idata == 0 into the register.
 783: for nm, off, pre, want in (("genctl", GENCTL, "0x82", "0x82"), ("t2ctl", T2CTL, "0x03", "0x3"),
 784:                            ("t2icr", T2ICR, "0x13", "0x13"), ("scctx", SCCTX, "0x1f", "0x1f")):
 785:     t, alive, how = session(setup(r5=pre) + program([ST_B(5, off), LD_H(4, off), LD_BU(4, off)]) + ["print r4"])
 786:     row("hrd %s rb" % nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", want,
 787:         "%s unchanged after a wide READ -- the arm's write-side body must not run on a read" % nm.upper())
 788: t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([I_ST_SCR, LD_H(4, IPL), I_LD_SCR]))
 789: row("hrd ipl noro", t.count("write to read-only PCCTWO_IPL"), 0,
 790:     "a wide READ of IPL never reaches the write body's read-only print")
 791: 
 792: #  PASS 6 (grok named it; both Agent seats measured the neighbouring cells): BYTE reads reach
 793: #  EVERY arm -- the six odd blocks too, since a byte access skips the alignment check -- and
 794: #  fall through the width guard to the arm's second predicate.  Delete it at a storing block
 795: #  and a byte READ stores idata == 0; the readback in the same instruction stream is served by
 796: #  the memcpy before the switch and still prints the old value.  So: set a byte, read it, read
 797: #  it AGAIN.  Guest path at every block, even and odd alike.
 798: for nm, off, pre, want in (("genctl", GENCTL, "0x82", "0x82"), ("vecbase", VECBASE, "0x50", "0x50"),
 799:                            ("t2ctl", T2CTL, "0x03", "0x3"), ("t2icr", T2ICR, "0x13", "0x13"),
 800:                            ("sccicr", SCCICR, "0x1f", "0x1f"), ("scctx", SCCTX, "0x1f", "0x1f"),
 801:                            ("sccrx", SCCRX, "0x1f", "0x1f"), ("scsiicr", SCSIICR, "0x1f", "0x1f"),
 802:                            ("mask", MASK, "0x12", "0x12")):
 803:     t, alive, how = session(setup(r5=pre) + program([ST_B(5, off), LD_BU(4, off), LD_BU(4, off)]) + ["print r4"])
 804:     row("brd2 " + nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", want,
 805:         "%s unchanged after TWO byte READS -- the arm's write body must not run on a byte read" % nm.upper())
 806: t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([LD_BU(4, PSCALEADJ), LD_BU(4, PSCALEADJ)]))
 807: row("brd pscale noig", t.count("PSCALEADJ ignored"), 0, "byte READS of PSCALEADJ never reach the write body's print")
 808: t, alive, how = session(setup() + program([LD_BU(4, IPL), LD_BU(4, IPL)]))
 809: row("brd ipl noro", t.count("write to read-only PCCTWO_IPL"), 0, "byte READS of IPL never reach the write body's read-only print")
 810: 
 811: def c040ok(v):
 812:     #  pass 8 (Opus F16): a value whose landing lane carries PCC2_C040 (0x04) would kill the
 813:     #  host through reassert_interrupts() instead of landing -- the row would still red, by
 814:     #  death, and the NOROW line below would be false.  Refuse such a lane at authoring time.
 815:     assert (int(v, 16) & 0xff) & 0x04 == 0, "GENCTL lane %s carries PCC2_C040" % v
 816:     return v
 817: #  PASS 6, the LANDING channel at len 4 and len 8 (Opus seat, M1_W4FALL_ALL: `break;' ->
 818: #  `if (len < 4) break;' at all twelve scored 118/118).  `latch all w' and `latch all d' count
 819: #  the ANNOUNCE; nothing read the register back after a 4- or 8-byte write, so a guard that
 820: #  announces and then lets the wide value land was invisible.  One readback per storing block
 821: #  per width; the two print-only bodies counted at zero; SCCERR is E.
 822: #  PASS 13 (GPT-6 Astra fix review): five arms test their HUH? bits on the COMPOSED idata --
 823: #  VECBASE `& ~0xf0', SCCICR/SCCTX `& ~0x1f', SCCRX/SCSIICR `& ~0xdf' -- and every wide value
 824: #  the rows drive at them (0x0303, 0xaab8, the rb4/rb8 lanes) has those bits SET, so a guard
 825: #  `&& (idata & ~mask)' would decline every existing row and LAND a HUH?-clear wide write.
 826: #  One halfword within the mask per arm, appended to the rb4 session; each lands to a value
 827: #  the preset is not (0xf0 vs 0x50; 0x10 vs 0x1f; 0x01 vs 0x1f).
 828: HUHQ = {VECBASE: "0x00f0", SCCICR: "0x0010", SCCTX: "0x0010", SCCRX: "0x0001", SCSIICR: "0x0001"}
 829: for nm, off, pre, want in (("genctl", GENCTL, "0x82", "0x82"), ("vecbase", VECBASE, "0x50", "0x50"),
 830:                            ("t2ctl", T2CTL, "0x03", "0x3"), ("t2icr", T2ICR, "0x13", "0x13"),
 831:                            ("sccicr", SCCICR, "0x1f", "0x1f"), ("scctx", SCCTX, "0x1f", "0x1f"),
 832:                            ("sccrx", SCCRX, "0x1f", "0x1f"), ("scsiicr", SCSIICR, "0x1f", "0x1f"),
 833:                            ("mask", MASK, "0x12", "0x12")):
 834:     #  pass 7 (Opus seat, measured in part6b/M_W4FALL_ALL.out): at GENCTL the lanes 0xdd and
 835:     #  0x44 carry bit 0x04 = PCC2_C040, so a LANDED write there ends the host (pcc2c040kill)
 836:     #  and the row killed by death, not by value.  GENCTL gets lanes with bit 2 clear.
 837:     w4 = c040ok("0xaab8ccd9") if off == GENCTL else "0xaab8ccdd"
 838:     w8 = c040ok("0xaab8ccdd00112240") if off == GENCTL else "0xaab8ccdd00112244"
 839:     t, alive, how = session(setup(r5=pre) + program([ST_B(5, off)]) + ["put w 0x%x, %s" % (PCC2 + off, w4)]
 840:                             + program([LD_BU(4, off)], at=CODE + 0x100) + ["print r4"]
 841:                             + ((["put h 0x%x, %s" % (PCC2 + off, HUHQ[off])] + program([LD_BU(4, off)], at=CODE + 0x200)
 842:                                 + ["print r4"]) if off in HUHQ else []))
 843:     row("rb4 " + nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", want,
 844:         "%s unchanged after a declined 4-byte write -- the refusal, not the announce" % nm.upper())
 845:     if off in HUHQ:
 846:         q = re.findall(r"print\s+r4\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)", t)
 847:         row("rbq " + nm, (("0x%x" % int(q[1], 16)) if len(q) > 1 else "short-transcript (FAILED FOR SOME OTHER REASON)") if alive else "died", want,
 848:             "%s unchanged after a HUH?-CLEAR wide write (%s, no bit outside the arm's mask) -- `&& (idata & ~mask)' would land it (pass 13)" % (nm.upper(), HUHQ[off]))
 849:     t, alive, how = session(setup(r5=pre) + program([ST_B(5, off)]) + ["put d 0x%x, %s" % (PCC2 + off, w8)]
 850:                             + program([LD_BU(4, off)], at=CODE + 0x100) + ["print r4"])
 851:     row("rb8 " + nm, printed(t, "r4") if alive else "died", want,
 852:         "%s unchanged after a declined 8-byte write" % nm.upper())
 853: t, alive, how = session(["put w 0x%x, 0xaab8ccdd" % (PCC2 + PSCALEADJ)])
 854: row("pscale noig4", t.count("PSCALEADJ ignored"), 0, "a declined 4-byte write never reaches the PSCALEADJ print")
 855: t, alive, how = session(["put d 0x%x, 0xaab8ccdd00112244" % (PCC2 + PSCALEADJ)])
 856: row("pscale noig8", t.count("PSCALEADJ ignored"), 0, "a declined 8-byte write never reaches the PSCALEADJ print")
 857: t, alive, how = session(["put w 0x%x, 0xaab8ccdd" % (PCC2 + IPL)])
 858: row("ipl noig4", t.count("write to read-only PCCTWO_IPL"), 0, "a declined 4-byte write never reaches the IPL print")
 859: t, alive, how = session(["put d 0x%x, 0xaab8ccdd00112244" % (PCC2 + IPL)])
 860: row("ipl noig8", t.count("write to read-only PCCTWO_IPL"), 0, "a declined 8-byte write never reaches the IPL print")
 861: t, alive, how = session(["put w 0x%x, 0xaab8ccdd" % (PCC2 + MASK)] * 2)
 862: row("latch samew", t.count(DECL), 1, "two 4-byte writes to MASK announce ONCE -- the latch is not keyed by width")
 863: t, alive, how = session(["put d 0x%x, 0xaab8ccdd00112244" % (PCC2 + MASK)] * 2)
 864: row("latch samed", t.count(DECL), 1, "two 8-byte writes to MASK announce ONCE")
 865: #  pass 7 (Opus seat): a value-test QUALIFIER `&& idata != 1' on the guard lets wide writes of
 866: #  the value 1 land, and no row wide-wrote that value -- every value-test guard is caught only
 867: #  for the values rows drive.  (The bare SWAP `len != 1' -> `idata != 1' drops the length test
 868: #  and is killed by every byte preset: MEASURED 95/171 in part 7.)  Twelve 2-byte writes of
 869: #  0x0001: any arm whose guard exempts that value lands one.
 870: t, alive, how = session(["put h 0x%x, 0x0001" % (PCC2 + o) for _, o in BLOCKS12])
 871: row("latch all one", t.count(DECL), 12, "twelve 2-byte writes of the VALUE 1 -- an `idata != 1' guard lands one and drops the count")
 872: 
 873: #  PASS 6, the fix's guard qualified by a TIMER PENDING COUNT (both Agent seats measured it:
 874: #  `&& !d->pending_timer2_interrupts' and `&& d->pending_timer1_interrupts == 0' at the TxICR
 875: #  guard each scored 118/118).  pending_timer* is INCREMENTED only by pcc_timer_tick, a
 876: #  timer_add/SIGALRM callback -- which debugger.c stops for the whole of every `step' -- so no
 877: #  stepping row can ever hold it non-zero.  These rows ARM a timer (compare 1, count 0, IEN,
 878: #  CEN) and FREE-RUN to a breakpoint: the guest polls TxICR with `bb0 5, r4, -1' until
 879: #  reassert_interrupts() sets the INT bit, which happens ONLY under pending > 0 -- so the 0x31
 880: #  read after the loop is both the liveness control (the loop exited) and the device signature
 881: #  (a mis-encoded bb0 would read 0x11).  Then the wide write, with the count non-zero.
 882: T1CMP, T1COUNT, T2CMP, T2COUNT = 0x04, 0x08, 0x0c, 0x10
 883: def BB0(b5, rs, d16): return enc(0x34, b5, rs, d16)      # bb0 b5, rs, d16 (word displacement)
 884: def program_free(insns, at=CODE):
 885:     words = list(insns) + [I_BR_SELF, 0]
 886:     cmds = ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * i, w) for i, w in enumerate(words)]
 887:     return cmds + ["pc=0x%x" % at, "breakpoint add 0x%x" % (at + 4 * len(insns)), ("continue", 20.0, "BREAKPOINT")]
 888: def pend_arm(cmp_off, cnt_off, icr_off, ctl_off):
 889:     return [ST_W(5, cmp_off), ST_W(6, cnt_off), ST_B(7, icr_off), ST_B(8, ctl_off), LD_BU(4, icr_off), BB0(5, 4, -1)]
 890: PEND_REGS = ["r5=0x1", "r6=0x0", "r7=0x11", "r8=0x1", "r9=0x0", "r10=0x13", "r11=0x18", "r12=0x20", "r13=0x3"]   # r10/r11/r12: the IEN-set, ICLR-set and HUH-bit wide-write values (passes 10, 11)
 891: def cval(alive, how, val):
 892:     #  pass 8 (codex, grok): a decl/rb row graded after a missed breakpoint must say so;
 893:     #  pass 9 (codex): so must one graded after the guest died under the session.
 894:     if not alive: return "died (FAILED FOR SOME OTHER REASON)"
 895:     return "no-breakpoint (FAILED FOR SOME OTHER REASON)" if how == "no-breakpoint" else val
 896: def armval(t, alive, r4s):
 897:     #  pass 7 (codex, grok): a row must fail for the reason under test or say otherwise.
 898:     if not alive: return "died"
 899:     if "BREAKPOINT" not in t: return "no-breakpoint (FAILED FOR SOME OTHER REASON)"
 900:     return ("0x%x" % int(r4s[0], 16)) if r4s else "absent"
