The helpers return three separate observations: captured output, whether a PTY failure was observed, and the child’s exit status. `exit0` comes from that last one. Several probes assert a value produced after the access; others check only a diagnostic printed before a possible exit. I’m separating protection within the same session from coverage supplied by another session.
