397: #
398: #  The header's ban on the survival channel was written too broadly.  Reinstating `exit(1)`
399: #  after the fatal() PRINTS THE DIAGNOSTIC AND THEN DIES: the message count is 1, the byte
400: #  is right, and a presence-only row is GREEN on a verbatim reinstatement of the very defect
401: #  this round removed.  The witness measured exactly that shape pre-fix -- `a88 says` = 1
402: #  AND `a88 kill` = exit1, in the same session.
403: #
404: #  THE CORRECT RULE: survival is a dead channel for rows pinning the ACCEPT side, because
405: #  the fix makes accepted values survive either way.  On the DECLINE side it is the ONLY
406: #  channel that sees clause (b).  So a decline row asserts BOTH -- announced, and survived.
407: A = Addr(CODE)
